From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:57:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] feat(mcp): list only seen events from read-data-schema

On the friction project, 66 of 71 rows of the events listing were
PostHog's catalogue of known events the project never sent, about 3,000
tokens around 5 real events (B2).

read-data-schema now leaves out the rows the backend marks "(not seen in
the last N days)" and reports them as a count with the call that lists
them: query.include_unseen = true. The option is stripped before the
request, so the backend helper and its formatting are unchanged; only
the events kind is filtered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
